WEBVTT

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:10.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the 30th. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.939 --> 00:00:16.839
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, you're on. Before we start, though—the football last night. What was that about?</v>

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.789
<v Callum Reid>Some of us are trying to forget it, mate.</v>

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:24.890
<v Jamie Brennan>Fair enough. That's the football review finished, then.</v>

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:33.350
<v Hannah Price>Whose new car is that in the car park? The shiny one taking up most of the view.</v>

00:00:34.869 --> 00:00:40.469
<v Marcus Hale>I saw that coming in. Parked miles from everyone else. Clearly hasn't met our pigeons yet.</v>

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.920
<v Hannah Price>Give it a week. It'll look like the rest of ours.</v>

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:50.609
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get onto pigeon damage—finished bits first, then what's actually still open.</v>

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:57.740
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah so, I already swapped the filter on the line 3 screw yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.770
<v Callum Reid>Right, that was the one I remembered being on the list.</v>

00:01:03.439 --> 00:01:06.939
<v Marcus Hale>Was on it, yeah. Not another filter change for today.</v>

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:12.930
<v Hannah Price>And I signed off the inspection on the Forklift Fleet on Tuesday. That's closed as well.</v>

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. Both finished, not carry-overs.</v>

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:22.579
<v Sarah Okafor>I tested the line 3 chiller yesterday and it's all fine now. Nothing further on that.</v>

00:01:23.829 --> 00:01:28.730
<v Aisha Begum>Good. Easy to lose the actual work under all the old entries, isn't it?</v>

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:36.859
<v Hannah Price>One observation, not a job: I noticed the relief valve was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.180
<v Marcus Hale>Settled back down, did it? Not still running warm?</v>

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:46.560
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, settled down. Just passing on what I saw, no new action.</v>

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:53.359
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. The permit to work and isolation for the guard switch on two—that still needs sorting.</v>

00:01:55.730 --> 00:02:04.829
<v Jamie Brennan>I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the guard switch on two by the end of the week. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie. Agreed, by the end of the week, not an urgent one.</v>

00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:18.210
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah. That's me sorting the permit and isolation, just to be clear.</v>

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:23.150
<v Aisha Begum>Understood. Not recording that as you replacing the switch as well.</v>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:30.289
<v Fiona Doyle>While we're on the open bits, I'll grease and check the bearings on the main conveyor this morning.</v>

00:02:32.449 --> 00:02:36.650
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, you clipped out a bit. Grease and check the bearings, both?</v>

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:42.030
<v Fiona Doyle>Both, yeah. I'll grease and check them this morning.</v>

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Got you, Fiona. Main conveyor, this morning.</v>

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:54.270
<v Marcus Hale>On my side, I can't get to the dryer until production gives us a window. Still blocked.</v>

00:02:55.039 --> 00:02:58.889
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, there's no window available. That's where we are with it.</v>

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:05.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, dryer stays blocked. We're not agreeing a start or handing out another job on that here.</v>

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:15.289
<v Marcus Hale>And we were going to replace the belt on the palletiser, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:03:17.479 --> 00:03:22.379
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, not part of today's agreed work. That one keeps cropping up in conversation.</v>

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:29.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. I'll replace the seals on the PRV on the boiler after lunch. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.849
<v Marcus Hale>Just the seals on that one, yeah?</v>

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, the seals. I'll do that after lunch.</v>

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:45.900
<v Jamie Brennan>Okay, Saz on the seals for the PRV on the boiler. Normal priority, got it.</v>

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:57.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus Hale, can you do a site visit at Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor on the 3rd? Whenever you get a chance on that date; it's not a rush one.</v>

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:04.539
<v Marcus Hale>Ah, no, sorry. I can't do the 3rd. You'll have to give that one to someone else.</v>

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:15.930
<v Sarah Okafor>All right. Fiona, can you take that instead—do a site visit at Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor on the 3rd? Whenever you get a chance on the day.</v>

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:26.939
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll take that instead. I'll do the site visit at Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor on the 3rd, whenever I get a chance that day.</v>

00:04:28.209 --> 00:04:32.759
<v Fiona Doyle>Separate from the main conveyor this morning, obviously. Two different entries for me.</v>

00:04:34.089 --> 00:04:37.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, Fiona. Bearings this morning; site visit on the 3rd. Agreed.</v>

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.089
<v Hannah Price>You could borrow the shiny car for the visit. Arrive looking terribly important.</v>

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:49.790
<v Marcus Hale>Only if you're allowed within ten feet of it. I reckon there's an exclusion zone.</v>

00:04:51.209 --> 00:04:56.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Behave. Um, I'll swap the filter on the AC1 at half two. It's urgent.</v>

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.990
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry—talked over the end there. At half two, and urgent?</v>

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:08.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, at half two. I'll swap it then; it's urgent, not one to slide.</v>

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.000
<v Jamie Brennan>Got it, Saz. AC1 filter, at half two, urgent.</v>

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:21.560
<v Marcus Hale>And that's separate from my line 3 screw filter, which is already done. Similar wording, different bit of kit.</v>

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:29.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Last one from me: I'll run a function test on the Fire Alarm Panel this afternoon.</v>

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.120
<v Hannah Price>Top priority please, that one.</v>

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:40.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. I'll take the Fire Alarm Panel function test as top priority this afternoon.</v>

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:50.629
<v Fiona Doyle>For the record, that's Sarah Okafor on the Fire Alarm Panel, this afternoon, top priority. Same person we've called Saz on the other two.</v>

00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:55.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, still only one of me, unfortunately. That's agreed.</v>

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.399
<v Callum Reid>Clear enough. Two filter jobs mentioned, but only the AC1 one is still open.</v>

00:06:03.379 --> 00:06:08.629
<v Marcus Hale>Correct. Line 3 screw done yesterday, and the palletiser belt isn't in today's work either.</v>

00:06:09.269 --> 00:06:14.870
<v Hannah Price>And my relief valve comment was only an observation. Forklift Fleet inspection is already signed off.</v>

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:25.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Quick check before we go. Jamie, permit to work and isolation for the guard switch on two by the end of the week. Matters, but not urgent.</v>

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.519
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll sort that. End of the week.</v>

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:41.829
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, grease and check the bearings on the main conveyor this morning, and Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor on the 3rd, whenever you get a chance that day.</v>

00:06:42.329 --> 00:06:46.529
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, agreed to both. I've got the visit instead of Marcus Hale.</v>

00:06:48.149 --> 00:06:57.949
<v Sarah Okafor>And mine: seals on the PRV on the boiler after lunch, normal priority; AC1 filter at half two, urgent; Fire Alarm Panel function test this afternoon, top priority.</v>

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:04.470
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, that's clear. Nothing from the finished or blocked bits has sneaked into that.</v>

00:07:05.819 --> 00:07:07.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. That's us.</v>
